 on Python 3.8 fails when running this function call:\r\n```py\r\n    console_scripts(\r\n        str(destination_path),\r\n        {\"entrypoint\": \"zimports\", \"options\": \"-e\"},\r\n        ignore_output=ignore_output,\r\n    )\r\n```\r\n\r\nThis happens, because the code assumes (write_hooks.py:141), that the returned object `EntryPoint` has a `module` or `attr` property (which it has on 3.9, but not on 3.8).\r\n```py\r\n        [\r\n            sys.executable,\r\n            \"-c\",\r\n            \"import %s; %s.%s()\" % (impl.module, impl.module, impl.attr),\r\n        ]\r\n```\r\n\r\nThe difference between the two versions are the different imports in compat.py:32:\r\n```py\r\nif py38:\r\n    from importlib import metadata as importlib_metadata\r\nelse:\r\n    import importlib_metadata  # type:ignore[no-redef] # noqa\r\n```\r\n**Error**\r\n```\r\nC:\\Users\\krumm-ti\\Documents\\PycharmProjects\\alembic\\venv\\Scripts\\python.exe C:/Users/krumm-ti/Documents/PycharmProjects/alembic/tools/write_pyi.py\r\nTraceback (most recent call last):\r\n  File \"C:/Users/krumm-ti/Documents/PycharmProjects/alembic/tools/write_pyi.py\", line 199, in <module>\r\n    main(args)\r\n  File \"C:/Users/krumm-ti/Documents/PycharmProjects/alembic/tools/write_pyi.py\", line 173, in main\r\n    run_file(\r\n  File \"C:/Users/krumm-ti/Documents/PycharmProjects/alembic/tools/write_pyi.py\", line 146, in run_file\r\n    generate_pyi_for_proxy(\r\n  File \"C:/Users/krumm-ti/Documents/PycharmProjects/alembic/tools/write_pyi.py\", line 75, in generate_pyi_for_proxy\r\n    console_scripts(\r\n  File \"C:\\Users\\krumm-ti\\Documents\\PycharmProjects\\alembic\\venv\\lib\\site-packages\\alembic\\script\\write_hooks.py\", line 145, in console_scripts\r\n    \"import %s; %s.%s()\" % (impl.module, impl.module, impl.attr),\r\nAttributeError: 'EntryPoint' object has no attribute 'module'\r\n```\r\n\r\n**Versions.**\r\n - OS: Windows 10\r\n - Python: 3.8/3.9\r\n - Alembic: current master\r\n - SQLAlchemy:\r\n - Database:\r\n - DBAPI:\r\n\r\n**Additional context**\r\n<!-- Add any other context about the problem here. -->\r\n\r\n**Have a nice day!**\r\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/alembic/issues/915/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/alembic/issues/915/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed"}},"event":"cross-referenced"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/alembic/issues/comments/931082051","html_url":"https://github.com/sqlalchemy/alembic/issues/934#issuecomment-931082051","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/alembic/issues/934","id":931082051,"node_id":"IC_kwDOCX47u843fy9D","user":{"login":"CaselIT","id":16175304,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MTc1MzA0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16175304?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/CaselIT","html_url":"https://github.com/CaselIT","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CaselIT/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CaselIT/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CaselIT/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CaselIT/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CaselIT/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CaselIT/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CaselIT/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CaselIT/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CaselIT/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2021-09-30T08:58:19Z","updated_at":"2021-09-30T08:58:19Z","body":"The issue can be solved by installing `importlib_metadata` also on 3.8.\r\n\r\nI wonder why the test did not catch it. I guess we need to add a covering case for this","author_associati